# Serena QA then ship (Staging-first — critical)

This rule is **mandatory** for every agent on `pavilion`. It overrides “only commit/push when asked” and overrides any habit of going straight to production.

After a complete, shippable **application** change, run Serena QA.

If Serena fails: fix and re-run. Do not commit, deploy, or push.

If Serena passes (diagnostics clean, scoped to the task), do this **exact** order:

## Stone Hill (`www.shmspto.org`)

Stone Hill production deploys from **`auraflux-dev/shmspto`** via treasurer Git integration. See **`shms-deploy-git.mdc`** and **`shms-edit-home.mdc`**.

**Edit in `~/shmspto` first.** Do not leave school site / portal / staff changes only in this monorepo.

1. **Commit** in the **`shmspto` repo**. Do **not** push `pavilion` `main` for Stone Hill prod.
2. **`node scripts/shms-frontend-parity.mjs`**. If school-facing files are only in the monorepo, port them into `shmspto` before calling the ship done.
3. **Staging review** (visitor-facing): confirm **https://shmspto.vercel.app** when staging is current. **STOP** for Rob OK (`looks good`, `ship it`, `go live`, `OK`, etc.).
4. **`git push origin main`** on `auraflux-dev/shmspto`. Treasurer Vercel **`frontend`** auto-deploys. Agents do **not** run `vercel deploy --prod` locally (no treasurer login).
5. **`node scripts/check-prod-deploy.mjs`** from the `shmspto` repo. Done means checks pass on https://www.shmspto.org, not just GitHub green.

**Staff-only** Stone Hill (`/staff`, `app/api/staff`, staff UI with no visitor copy change): skip Rob wait. Push `shmspto` `main` after Serena QA, then run the check script.

## Pavilion (this monorepo)

- **Commit** task files on `pavilion` (do not push Stone Hill via this repo).
- Pavilion marketing → `commons-site` (`onpavilion.com`).
- Pavilion demo/trial → `commons-pto-demo` / `commons-pto` as relevant.
- Default: after a Stone Hill ship, also ship Pavilion from the same product change when it applies (vanilla only). Skip for clearly SHMS-only work or if Rob says skip.
- Never deploy from a dirty working tree. Never mix Stone Hill and Pavilion env.

## Exceptions

- **Rules / docs / memories only** (no application runtime): commit on `pavilion`, then push `pavilion` `main`. Skip deploy checks.
- Never include unrelated WIP, secrets, Budget/Plaid/terminal/spirit-wear/`tmp` unless they are the task.
- Never mix Stone Hill and Pavilion env (DATABASE_URL, Wix, Square, Stripe).

## Anti-patterns (forbidden)

- Pushing `pavilion` `main` and calling Stone Hill “shipped.”
- Editing Stone Hill Staff / portal / site only under `pavilion/frontend` without porting to `~/shmspto`.
- `vercel deploy --prod` for Stone Hill from agent shells (`robert-4220` or treasurer).
- Deploying Stone Hill from `robert-4220s-projects`.
- Calling the task “live” when `check-prod-deploy.mjs` has not passed.
- Asking Rob to review on a one-off `frontend-xxxxx.vercel.app` Preview URL.
- Skipping staging for public visitor changes by labeling them “staff-related.”

## Staging URL (Stone Hill)

https://shmspto.vercel.app

Google / Wix OAuth redirect URIs must include this host (see `scripts/google-workspace-admin-setup.md`).
